WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.341
Nobody taught you how money works in school.

00:00:02.541 --> 00:00:05.051
But it affects every decision you'll ever make.

00:00:05.251 --> 00:00:07.489
Let's fix that in sixty seconds.

00:00:07.689 --> 00:00:12.493
Financial literacy is simply knowing how to earn, spend, save, and grow your money.

00:00:12.693 --> 00:00:15.399
Start with one rule: spend less than you earn.

00:00:15.599 --> 00:00:19.748
It sounds obvious, but most people never track where their money goes.

00:00:19.948 --> 00:00:22.485
Try the fifty, thirty, twenty rule.

00:00:22.685 --> 00:00:26.522
Fifty percent of your income goes to needs, like rent and food.

00:00:26.722 --> 00:00:28.628
Thirty percent goes to wants.

00:00:28.828 --> 00:00:31.801
Twenty percent goes to savings and debt payoff.

00:00:32.001 --> 00:00:35.945
Build an emergency fund that covers three to six months of expenses.

00:00:36.145 --> 00:00:38.318
And pay off high-interest debt first.

00:00:38.518 --> 00:00:42.203
Credit card interest can cost you more than your investments earn.

00:00:42.403 --> 00:00:44.124
Then let time work for you.

00:00:44.324 --> 00:00:48.240
Compound interest means your money earns money, and that money earns more.

00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:51.977
Starting small today beats starting big ten years from now.

00:00:52.177 --> 00:00:54.357
You don't need to be rich to learn this.

00:00:54.557 --> 00:00:56.058
You just need to start.

00:00:56.258 --> 00:00:58.795
Follow for more money lessons they never taught you.
